##### 10. Ignored / Disabled Test — `disabledTest()`

**Line 109.** `@Disabled("flaky, fix later")` — the reason is vague and has no tracking ticket.

```java
@Disabled("flaky, fix later")
void disabledTest() { ... }
```

**Fix:** Either fix the flakiness (the test body looks deterministic — it should not be flaky) or link a ticket:

```java
@Disabled("Tracked by PROJ-1234 — investigating intermittent CI failure")
```

If the test is actually stable, remove `@Disabled` and let it run.

**Risk if unfixed:** Dead test that will never be revisited; the underlying issue silently rots.

